extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market printed 75-77 (cache p076-p078, page_offset 1). The entry Kryygorth''s Lesson opens in the right column of printed 75 after the Kryygorth Hunter; the R.C.C. block runs from the foot of 75 through the left column of 76 to the right column of 77, where the Kryygorth Pegasus begins. Printed 76 and 77 read off 170 dpi renders on 2026-11-19; every figure below matches the render. The text layer sets M.D.C. 6D6x10 as 6D6xlO, S.D.C. 1D6x10+60 as lD6x 10+60, P.P.E. 4D6x10 as 4D6xlO, money 4D6x100 as 4D6xlOO and the value 2D6x10 million as 2D6xlO, and drops the degree sign from the 90 cone (cache p077-p078). || NAME: id kryygorths-lesson; the heading is Kryygorth''s Lesson, the listing on 71 drops the possessive. || FORM: the Player Character Note opens the class to players only as an Emancipated Lesson, so this class is that form, per Nate''s 2026-11-18 ruling; the full creature is its creatures row. Every figure the page halves on emancipation is stored halved and the penalties block is applied. || ATTRIBUTES: mental attributes as printed (I.Q. 3D6+2, M.E. 3D6+2, M.A. 2D6+1). Physical attributes are printed P.S. 3D6+22, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+18, P.B. 1D6+1, Spd 4D6 and halved on emancipation; no stored roll halves a die, so each is stored as the roll closest to half the printed one in range and mean, fractions dropped: P.S. 3D3+10, P.P. 3D3-1, P.E. 3D3+8, P.B. 1D3, Spd 2D6. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. are prose. || POOLS: M.D.C. printed 6D6x10 plus 2D6 per level, halved to 3D6x10 plus 1D6 per level. P.P.E. printed 4D6x10 plus 4D6 per level, halved to 2D6x10 plus 2D6 per level. Horror Factor 9, the emancipated figure. The S.D.C.-world Hit Points and S.D.C. are stored as printed, in prose, because the page does not say they halve. || XP: the book names the Dragon experience table, so xp_table copies production''s dragon-hatchling row (read --remote 2026-11-19), per Nate''s 2026-09-26 ruling. || MAGIC: Lessons know all spell magic of levels 1-5, granted by name as every general invocation production held at spell levels 1-5 for Rifts (system rifts, both or unset; no tradition) on 2026-11-19, 105 spells. The additional 10+3D6 from levels 5-12 are a starting pick of 28, the most the roll allows, at spell levels 6-12 because every level 5 spell is already granted, with a note to roll and take only that many. An Emancipated Lesson learns one new spell per level after emancipation and nothing above level 12: spells_per_level 1 capped at spell levels 1-12. The page does not say an emancipated Lesson loses its spells, so they are kept. || COMBAT: the two bonus attacks (or magic attacks) are lost on emancipation and not stored. The one more at levels 6 and 12 is printed in the same sentence and the page does not say it is lost, so it is stored as printed. +4 strike and parry, +2 dodge, +2 roll as printed; the +3 initiative is not stored, because an Emancipated Lesson has no initiative bonus from any source (prose). +4 vs magic on spell_magic and ritual_magic; +2 vs psionics; +10% vs coma/death on coma_death_pct. Imperviousness to poison and disease is lost; the +2 vs poisons and disease is stored on toxins_poisons and disease. || SKILLS: base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus, less the 10% emancipation penalty on every R.C.C. skill. Languages: Dragonese and two of choice at 98%. Dragonese is stored 88% with per_level 0; the two of choice are a pick from Language: Other at bonus 38 (the row 50% +38 = 88%), which then rises 5% a level, because a language pick may not be frozen at a flat base (regression). Literacy: Dragonese is Literacy: Dragonese/Elven; the literacy of choice is a pick from Literacy: Other at +10. Lore: Demon and Monster is Lore: Demons & Monsters; Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic. Hand to Hand: Expert, upgraded to Martial Arts or Assassin for one related pick. The -10% on related and secondary skills is prose: the printed category bonuses are stored as printed. Related: seven at level one, one more at 3, 6, 9 and 12. Pilot is Hover Craft (ground) for hover vehicles (basic types only), and Horsemanship: Basic and/or Exotic Animals is Horsemanship: General and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals in the Horsemanship category, all +5%. Read Sensory Equipment is the catalog''s Sensory Equipment. Cowboy, Electrical, Mechanical and Military: none. Secondary: five at level one, one more at 4, 7 and 13, from the related list. || NATURAL ABILITIES: eye blasts up to 4D6 M.D. halved to 2D6; bio-regeneration 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, the emancipated figure. Dimensional teleport: the page''s (half when emancipated) follows the four attempts every 24 hours and is read as halving the attempts to two; the 44% +4% per level is stored as printed. || MONEY: none for slaves; Emancipated Lessons start with 4D6x100 credits. || EQUIPMENT: utility belt, backpack, bedroll and canteen granted; the energy weapon, ancient weapon, provisions and odds and ends are unnamed and are prose. || VALUE: a Lesson usually sells for 2D6x10 million credits, often twice that; none has been sold at the Splynn market."
