## Lore

The Lessons were once a small, slender and clever people of dimensional raiders, on their way to a name as feared as the Temporal Raiders, until a handful of them stole from the Splugorth Lord Kryygorth. He had his minions enslave the whole race and kill any who resisted; of fewer than ten million, about four million survived to be handed to his Bio-Wizards. Decades of transmutation killed more than half of those. What came out were massive, bloated, supernaturally strong humanoids with amplified magic and far more P.P.E., a crippled talent for dimensional teleport, and no free will: Kryygorth''s "lesson" to the Megaverse.

A Lesson must bond to a master at birth or die within hours. While linked it obeys every order, even to kill itself, and cannot act against its master in the smallest way; it can be forbidden to speak to anyone and ordered to kill anyone who tries to free it. Ownership can pass to another, but the Lesson goes free only when its master dies.

Freed Lessons, called Emancipated Lessons, are truly rare: most were freed by accident by heroes settling a score with their masters, and a few arranged it themselves through cunning and patience. They pay for it. Within 24 hours of the break their great powers fade, their bodies shrink to six or seven feet and run to fat, their supernatural attributes and M.D.C. halve, and they become indecisive and slow to act. Many are bitter and vengeful toward their old masters and the Splugorth, and must relearn how to live free.

Fewer than a million Lessons are thought to exist, a fifth of them owned by the Splugorth; Lord Splynncryth owns a hundred, all linked to him. Fewer than a hundred are on Rifts Earth, most in Atlantis. Their homeworld is unknown and may have been destroyed. Free Lessons join anybody, feel a kinship with creatures of magic and dimensional travelers, and a few have joined the Liberated Underground to strike back at the Splugorth.

## Value

Very rare, very powerful and absolutely controllable, a Lesson usually sells for 2D6x10 million credits and often for twice that. The Splugorth do not like to keep them and sell them whenever practical, but none is known to have been sold at the Splynn Dimensional Market.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kryygorths-lesson');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kryygorths-lesson';

